%I A399638 #5 Sep 09 2026 10:55:47
%S A399638 1,2,2,3,4,5,9,21,65,286,1714,13378,134056,1720761
%N A399638 Number of nonisomorphic right-Euclidean relations on n elements having trivial automorphism group.
%C A399638 A connected right-Euclidean relation is rigid if and only if its nonempty out-neighborhoods of nonreflexive elements are distinct and, regarded as the edges of a simple hypergraph on the unique nonempty reflexive equivalence class, form a hypergraph with trivial automorphism group.
%F A399638 Let Omega_k = 2^[k] \ {emptyset}. For k >= 1, define H_k(y) = Sum_{[K] <= S_k} mu(1,K)/|N_{S_k}(K)| * Product_{O in Omega_k/K} (1 + y^|O|), where the sum is over conjugacy classes of subgroups K of S_k, mu is the Möbius function of the subgroup lattice, N_{S_k}(K) is the normalizer of K in S_k, and O runs over the orbits of K on the nonempty subsets of [k].
%F A399638 Let q(s) = delta_{s,1} + Sum_{k=1..s} [y^(s-k)] H_k(y). Then Sum_{n>=0} a(n)*x^n = Product_{s>=1} (1 + x^s)^q(s).
%e A399638 For n = 6, the first polynomials are H_1(y) = 1+y, H_2(y) = y+y^2, and H_3(y) = y^2+3*y^3+3*y^4+y^5; also [y^j]H_4(y) = 0 for j = 0,1,2. Hence q(1),...,q(6) = 2,1,1,1,1,3. Therefore, up to degree 6, Product_{s>=1} (1+x^s)^q(s) = (1+x)^2*(1+x^2)*(1+x^3)*(1+x^4)*(1+x^5)*(1+x^6)^3 + O(x^7), whose coefficient of x^6 is 9. Thus a(6) = 9.
%Y A399638 Cf. A399636 (nonisomorphic connected right-Euclidean relations), A399637 (nonisomorphic right-Euclidean relations), A398718 (labeled right-Euclidean relations), A001831 (labeled connected case).
%K A399638 nonn,more,new
